   "id": "kiddushin.29b.8",
   "daf": "29b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "לְלַמְּדוֹ תּוֹרָה. מְנָלַן? דִּכְתִיב: ״וְלִמַּדְתֶּם אֹתָם אֶת בְּנֵיכֶם״. וְהֵיכָא דְּלָא אַגְמְרֵיהּ אֲבוּהּ מִיחַיַּיב אִיהוּ לְמִיגְמַר נַפְשֵׁיהּ, דִּכְתִיב: ״וּלְמַדְתֶּם״.",
   "en": "§ The baraita teaches that a father is obligated «to teach» his son «Torah.» The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive this requirement? «As it is written: “And you shall teach them [velimadtem] to your sons”» (Deuteronomy 11:19). «And» in a case «where his father did not teach him he is obligated to teach himself, as it is written,» i.e., the verse can be read with a different vocalization: «And you shall study [ulmadtem].»"
  }
 ],
